---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { company } from "../data/site";
import { abs, breadcrumbSchema, WEBSITE_ID } from "../lib/seo";

const effective = "October 3, 2026";
const effectiveIso = "2026-10-03";

const title = "Privacy Policy";
const description = `How ${company.name} handles the information you share through this website: what we collect, why, and how to ask us to delete it.`;

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "Privacy policy", path: "/privacy/" },
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": `${abs("/privacy/")}#webpage`,
    url: abs("/privacy/"),
    name: "Privacy policy",
    description,
    inLanguage: "en-US",
    isPartOf: { "@id": WEBSITE_ID },
    datePublished: effectiveIso,
  },
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <section class="section page-hero" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1 id="privacy-title" class="h1">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">The short version: we collect what you send us, use it only to reply, and never sell it.</p>
      <p class="subtle meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveIso}>{effective}</time></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--border section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <p>
          This policy explains how {company.name} ("we", "us") handles information collected through
          <a href="/">{company.url.replace(/^https?:\/\//, "")}</a> (the "site"). It applies to this marketing site only.
          Work we do for clients is covered by the contracts we sign with them.
        </p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <h3>Information you give us</h3>
        <p>When you use the contact form or email us, we receive the details you choose to share, which may include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your name, work email address and company name;</li>
          <li>your company website, if you provide it;</li>
          <li>your project type, budget range, timeline and message;</li>
          <li>a project plan summary, if you arrived from our project estimator.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Please do not send confidential or sensitive information through the form. If a project needs it, we will sign an NDA first and agree on a secure way to share it.</p>

        <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
        <p>
          Like most websites, the servers that host this site may record standard technical logs, such as IP address,
          browser type, the pages requested and the time of the request. These logs are used to keep the site secure and
          working, and are not used to build profiles of individual visitors.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          We do not use advertising cookies, third-party advertising trackers or cross-site tracking. We do not sell or
          share your information for targeted advertising. If we ever add analytics, we will choose a privacy-respecting
          option and update this policy first.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <p>We use the information you send us only to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>reply to your inquiry and arrange a discovery call;</li>
          <li>prepare a technical roadmap or proposal you asked for;</li>
          <li>keep a record of our conversation if we go on to work together.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not add you to a marketing list without your permission, and we do not sell your personal information.</p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          We share information only with service providers that help us run the site and our email, such as our hosting,
          email and form-processing providers, and only so they can provide that service to us. We may also disclose
          information if required by law. We do not share it with anyone for their own marketing.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep inquiry emails and form submissions for as long as they are useful for our conversation with you and
          for normal business records, and delete them when they are no longer needed or when you ask us to.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us at any time to access, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you. Depending
          on where you live, you may have additional rights under local privacy laws. Email
          <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> with the subject "Privacy request" and we will respond
          promptly. We will not treat you differently for making a request.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          We use reasonable safeguards, such as encrypted connections (HTTPS), access controls and multi-factor
          authentication on the accounts that hold your information. No method of transmission or storage is completely
          secure, but we work to protect what you share with us.
        </p>

        <h2>International visitors</h2>
        <p>
          We are a remote-first team, so information you send us may be processed in countries other than the one you
          live in. We handle it as described in this policy wherever it is processed.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>This site is intended for businesses and is not directed to children under 16. We do not knowingly collect their information.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change this policy, we will update it on this page and change the effective date above.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy or this policy? Email <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding-block: calc(var(--section-y) * 0.7) calc(var(--section-y) * 0.5);
  }
  .hero-inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    justify-items: start;
  }
  .meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
  }
  .prose > h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 1.6em;
  }
</style>
